You can set up a check against a database column where the value is equal to the color value. For example, if your color column is called color_value, you'd add an equality check like:

```
<br>if (!is_color_allowed($color)) {
  return false;
}
```

The key thing to check: make sure the color column actually stores distinct values (e.g., 'red' vs 'green'), or you'll get matches on every color. If you need to store color names as strings too, you'll need a separate column that maps to the color name.
